RLK
---

Minimal C99 library for 2D grid-based games and roguelikes.

Build:
  make                  # Build librlk.a
  make lint             # Static analysis (-Werror)
  make test             # Run unit tests
  make clean            # Remove build artifacts

Note: the Makefiles use BSD make. On Linux, use `bmake` or `pmake`
instead of GNU make.

Configuration:
  Copy config.mk.example to config.mk to customize CFLAGS or library paths.

Headers:
  rlk.h                # Umbrella header (includes all of the below)
  err.h                # Error handling
  hash.h               # Seed/coordinate hashing
  fmath.h              # Math helpers
  noise.h              # Noise generation (value, perlin, fbm)
  rng.h                # Deterministic PRNG (splitmix64)
  tilemap.h            # 2D grid with occupancy
  wg_nf.h              # Noise-field world generation
  wg_nf_modulator.h    # Voronoi modulation stage for wg_nf
  wg_ca.h              # Cellular Automata (caves, organic structures)
  wg_bsp.h             # Binary Space Partitioning (rooms + corridors)

Demos:
  demo/demo_tilemap_viewer.c  # Interactive terrain viewer (PXL)

